description:
**Job responsibilities** 




 1\. Cooperate with sales to visit customers, promote product technology and product




 usage plans;




 2\. Provide customers with robot application technical support, communicate and




 solve technical problems encountered by customers;




 3\. Assist customers in repairing product software and hardware failures, and train




 customers in daily operation, use, and maintenance;




 4\. Understand customer needs and on\-site problems, communicate with product




 managers and formulate feasible solutions;




 5\. Collect customer feedback and assist R\&D engineers to improve products。




**Requirement** 




 1\. Have local legal work status; computer\-related majors are preferred




 2\. More than 3 years of relevant experience in pre\-sales, after\-sales, and after\-sales maintenance;




 3\. Language ability;English/Chinese, able to communicate and correspond to local




 customers;




 4\. Understand basic electrical knowledge and motor drive control principles;




 5\. Familiar with Linux platform experience is preferred; working experience in




 robotics, such as ROS is preferred;




 6\. Can accept frequent short\-term business trips;




 7\. Work seriously and meticulously, have a strong sense of responsibility, and have




 pressure tolerance; have good communication/coordination skills; have a good sense




 of service and responsibility。




**Skill Requirement** 




 \- Linux system




 \- ROS rviz




 \- Agent Management




 \- Project Managemen

Since its establishment in 1997, HYPERTECH S.A. has been transforming its clients’ needs and delivering impactful solutions to complex technological and communication problems all over Europe. The company has undergone significant growth, especially in recent years, and taken on more resources to better accommodate the needs of EU organisations, cultural institutions and private businesses. We are looking to hire a highly motivated and talented individual with creativity, intellectual capacity and curiosity, dedication and team spirit.




**Business and Data Analyst**
**Job Description**
* Involved in different projects such as the development of websites, static and interactive infographics and data visualisation products;
* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams, including project managers, product owners, designers and developers to ensure successful project delivery;
* Facilitate workshops and interviews with stakeholders to understand their needs, challenges and objectives;
* Translate business requirements into clear and concise functional specifications and user stories;
* Analyse, understand and draw conclusions from provided data, so as to support the development of a product;
* Prepare and present reports, deliverables, findings and recommendations to clients and stakeholders.


**Job Requirements**
* Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Computer Science or a related field;
* Proven experience of 2\+ years in a similar role;
* Proficiency in gathering and documenting business requirements and creating functional specifications;
* Excellent analytical, data interpretation and problem\-solving skills;
* Experience in data visualisation and Business Intelligence (BI) practices and tools;
* Detail\-oriented with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple tasks in a fast\-paced, deadline\-driven environment;
* Strong communication and presentation skills;
* Fluency in English and Greek (written and spoken).


**We Offer**
* Opportunity to work with a highly talented and experienced team;
* Continuous mental and creative challenges in a learning and fun environment;
* An attractive compensation package.


 If you are interested to join the HYPERTECH team send your CV at: desk@hypertech.gr
